-- title:
--   Divisibility of a from low coefficients of u(X-a)ⁿ-Xⁿ
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring, let $n$ be a natural number whose image in $A$ is a unit, let $u \in A[[X]]$ be a power series whose constant coefficient is a unit, let $a$ be an element of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\pi \in A$ be arbitrary. Assume that for every $k < n$ the coefficient of $X^k$ in $u \cdot (X - C\,a)^n - X^n$ lies in the principal ideal generated by $\pi$, where $C\,a$ denotes the constant power series $a$. The conclusion is twofold: first, $a$ itself lies in the ideal generated by $\pi$; second, for every $k$ with $k + 2 \le n$, the coefficient of $X^k$ in $u \cdot (X - C\,a)^n - X^n$ lies in the ideal generated by $\pi a$. Note that the hypothesis is imposed on all coefficients in degrees $< n$, while the sharpened conclusion concerns only the degrees $\le n-2$; no hypothesis that $n \ge 1$ is required, since invertibility of $n$ in $A$ already forces it (a local ring is nonzero).
--
--   This is the elementary local step in a first-order expansion argument: divisibility of the low-degree coefficients of $u\cdot(X-a)^n - X^n$ by $\pi$ bounds the displacement $a$ by $\pi$, and then improves the bound on those coefficients to $\pi a$. It is used in the study of models of prolongations of places on modular curves, in the lemmas bounding the order of a residue in terms of a relation of the form $1 + (\text{something})$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_mem_span_of_coeff_mul_X_sub_C_pow_sub_X_pow_mem_span.lean

